   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let m(x) = ln(25 - x^2) / x. Consider the largest interval that contains x = 2 and on which m is continuous. How many integers does that interval contain?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "numeric",
      "mathjson": 4
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The logarithm requires 25 - x^2 > 0, so -5 < x < 5, and the denominator is zero at x = 0.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Subtract",
            25,
            [
               "Power",
               "x",
               2
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "m is a quotient of a logarithmic function and a polynomial, each continuous on its domain, so m is continuous on (-5, 0) U (0, 5).",
         "mathjson": 0
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The piece containing x = 2 is (0, 5), open at 0 because of the denominator and open at 5 because ln is undefined at 0.",
         "mathjson": 5
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The integers in (0, 5) are 1, 2, 3 and 4.",
         "mathjson": 4
      }
   ],
